Kernel 7.1 broke the radxa aic8800 dkms source in several ways:

1. "wifi: move action code from per-type frame structs" (08e6183ed256) moved
   action_code out of the per-type structs and made the action union anonymous.
   The pre-7.1 layout (mgmt->u.action.u.<struct>) fails to compile with
   "'struct <anonymous>' has no member named 'u'".

2. cfg80211 changed several ops (add_key/get_key/del_key/
   set_default_mgmt_key/add_station/del_station/change_station/get_station/
   dump_station) from taking a net_device to taking a wireless_dev (MLD
   support), and cfg80211_new_sta()/cfg80211_del_sta() now take a wireless_dev.
   The pre-7.1 handlers failed with "from incompatible pointer type".

3. <linux/of_gpio.h> was removed ("gpio: remove of_get_named_gpio() and
   <linux/of_gpio.h>", b6420bd5aa0c), breaking aic8800_btlpm/rfkill.c which
   included it without using it.

Apply from the driver root (the directory containing aic8800_fdrv/,
aic8800_btlpm/ and aic8800_bsp/):  patch -p1 -i <this file>

Signed-off-by: Juan Sanchez Fuentes <juanesf91@gmail.com>
Assisted-by: opencode:big-pickle

